            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A joining and levelling system suitable for being used in furniture and furnishing items (M) with a bottom (12) and at least one shoulder (11) positionable with respect to a floor (P) comprising, in combination, at least one front foot unit (14,114) and at least one rear foot unit (15,115), wherein each front and rear foot unit (14,15; 114,115) comprises at least one connection group (GC) and a blocking group (GB) of a joining device for stably interconnecting the bottom (12) and the at least one shoulder, wherein the connection group (GC) and the blocking group (GB) of the joining device can be actuated from the front with respect to the furniture, wherein the at least one front foot unit (14,114) and the at least one rear foot unit (15,115) are positioned beneath the bottom (12) and facing the at least one shoulder (11), wherein the bottom (12) and the at least one shoulder (11) do not rest on the floor, wherein the at least one front foot unit (14,114) and the at least one rear foot unit (15,115) are positioned in an identical body (16,116) for both the at least one front foot unit (14,114) and the at least one rear foot unit (15,115), and actuation rods (36) of the joining device are provided, arranged in the at least one rear foot unit (15,115), positioned between the at least one front foot unit (14,114) and the at least one rear foot unit (15,115).</p>
            </abstract>
